1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,525
Same question, different answer.

2
00:00:02,825 --> 00:00:04,300
Here's why.

3
00:00:05,317 --> 00:00:09,167
A language model gives every next
token a probability.

4
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,492
Then it rolls weighted dice.

5
00:00:12,117 --> 00:00:14,517
Temperature reshapes the odds first.

6
00:00:14,817 --> 00:00:18,367
Turn it down, and Paris goes to 99%.

7
00:00:18,983 --> 00:00:23,333
Turn it up to 2, and Lyon wins about
one roll in seventeen.

8
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:28,100
That's the creativity knob, and
also a source of mistakes.

9
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:31,700
It's why the same question can
get a different answer.
